# Tests

- Don't sleep in tests. Wait for the condition you need, or inject a fake clock.
- `pytest.raises` names the exact exception you expect, never `Exception` or `BaseException`.
- Every `skip` and `xfail` says why (`reason="..."`).
- One behavior per test, and its name says which: `test_<behavior>_when_<condition>`.
- Test public behavior, not private helpers or internals.
- Unit tests don't reach the network or the real clock.
- Delete a test that cannot fail, such as one that only asserts a mock it just configured.
- Give a test module a local `conftest.py` when its setup needs a scope of its own. Keep fixtures shared by sibling modules in the parent `conftest.py`.

Why: sleeps make tests slow and flaky; a broad `pytest.raises` passes on the wrong error; an unexplained skip is never revisited; tests tied to internals break on refactors and can miss regressions. Keep specialized setup near the tests that use it.

